; vnetcheck: the virtionet.device beta check. Run it from a Shell in the
; kit's drawer while netprof-host runs on the PC (see ReadMe):
;   Execute vnetcheck HOST <PC address> [SECS <seconds>]
; HOST is the PC as the Amiga sees it (with QEMU's user network, 10.0.2.2).
; Everything goes to RAM:vnetcheck.txt: send that file back.
.key HOST/A,SECS/K
.def SECS 60
FailAt 30
Echo "virtionet.device beta check, please wait about 3 minutes"
Echo "== vnetcheck" >RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Date >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Version >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Version DEVS:Networks/virtionet.device FULL >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Version bsdsocket.library FULL >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== netprof info" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof info >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== driver statistics" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
s2test 0 networks/virtionet.device stats >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== cpu" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof cpu >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== round trips" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof rtt <HOST> count=200 >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== download, every byte checked" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof soakrecv <HOST> secs=<SECS> quiet >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== upload, every byte checked" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof soaksend <HOST> secs=<SECS> quiet >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== many short connections" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof soakrtt <HOST> secs=30 quiet >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== one transfer, measured" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
netprof recv <HOST> mb=32 >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Echo "== summary" >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Search RAM:vnetcheck.txt "PASS " NONUM CASE >RAM:vnetcheck-sum.txt
Search RAM:vnetcheck.txt "FAIL" NONUM CASE >>RAM:vnetcheck-sum.txt
Type RAM:vnetcheck-sum.txt >>RAM:vnetcheck.txt
Type RAM:vnetcheck-sum.txt
Echo "Done. Please send RAM:vnetcheck.txt."
